course: dictionary
lesson: 3464
title: Fairly: two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word fairly has two main meanings, and the words around it show you which one is meant. Read the sentence first, then ask: what does fairly mean here?
explain: In «A judge runs a court case fairly», fairly means in a fair, equal way, following the rules. Try swapping in equally: "runs a court case equally" still makes sense, so this is the right meaning.
explain: In «The planet has fairly few craters», fairly means quite or rather, but not very. Try swapping in quite: "quite few craters" still makes sense, so this meaning fits here.
explain: The clues are the key. Fair treatment, rules and sharing point to the first meaning. A word like few, cold or big, which describes how much or how strong something is, points to the second.
fact: Fairly means in a fair, equal way, following the rules.
fact: Fairly can also mean quite or rather, but not very.
fact: «Everyone deserves to be treated kindly and fairly, however they look.» Here fairly means equally, with no one left out or treated worse.
fact: «It is fairly cold today» means it is quite cold, but not freezing.
fact: Fair is the adjective and fairly is the adverb, so fairly often describes how someone does something.
exercise: «A judge runs a court case fairly and decides the punishment.» What does fairly mean here? | Angrily | Very quickly | *In a fair, equal way, following the rules | Quite or rather, but not very
exercise: «The planet has fairly few craters.» What does fairly mean here? | In a fair, equal way | *Quite or rather, but not very, as in few craters | Quite or rather, but not very | Exactly
exercise: Share the sweets fairly between three friends. What does fairly mean? | Quite or rather | Very fast | *In equal shares | Without any sweets
test:
Everyone must play fairly and follow the rules. What does fairly mean? | Quite | *In a fair way, following the rules | Loudly | Slowly
It is fairly cold today, so take a coat. What does fairly mean? | Extremely cold | In an equal way | *Quite or rather, but not very | Not at all
exam:
Which sentence uses fairly to mean in a fair, equal way? | The cake was fairly big. | It is fairly cold today. | *Everyone deserves to be treated kindly and fairly. | The planet has fairly few craters.
